# Graphify Router

Canon: `AGENTS.md` § Tool Routing. Detail: `docs/agent-workflows/graphify-routine.md`.

## Trigger

Use `/graphify` when the task needs repo/codebase search, architecture, coupling, boundaries, cross-package paths, god-node traces, or exploration across multiple modules — and `graphify-out/graph.json` exists.

Skip when the user gave an exact file/symbol or the graph is absent and scope is a single known edit.

## Read order (graph exists)

1. `graphify query "<question>"` (or agent runs `/graphify query` pipeline)
2. `graphify path "A" "B"` / `graphify explain "X"`
3. `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` (god nodes, surprises — not full dump)
4. Raw grep / wide file reads only if 1–3 fail

Separate **EXTRACTED** vs **INFERRED** edges; confirm inferred coupling with imports/calls/tests before refactor.

## Maintain

- Rebuild: `/graphify <path>` (prefer `django_apps`, `src`, not whole repo unless user asks)
- After code-only session changes: `graphify update <path>` (AST, no LLM)
- Doc/image changes: `/graphify <path> --update` or full rebuild

Skill: user-attached `graphify` or `graphify install --platform cursor`.
